-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5910+) **Cleaned** several **old Python 2-style** BUG syntax patterns so modern Python 3 linters/parsers can inspect them while keeping Civ4 Python 2.4 compatibility. These **distracted** modern Python linters such as ruff and **prevented them from finding errors**. Removed these parser blockers, such as old comma-exception binding `except Exception, e:` (to the already existing `e = sys.exc_info()[1]` in [BugUtil.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/BugUtil.py) pattern) and the old compatibility fallback `True, False = 1, 0` (to an equivalent), which improves code quality. This allowed Ruff to surface and find a **real previously hidden bug** in BUG [configobj.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/configobj.py): `_handle_comment` used undefined `_a_to_u('# ')` instead of the correct `self._a_to_u('# ')`, which we then **fixed**. See also [KI#143](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#143---fixed-bug-configobj-comment-writer-used-undefined-_a_to_u-instead-of-correct-self_a_to_u-old-bug-syntax-had-prevented-ruff-from-seeing-the-bug).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5911+) **Python source encoding cleanup:** fixed Ruff E902 `stream did not contain valid UTF-8` errors in old BUG TechWindow Python files by converting them to UTF-8 in VS Code. UTF-8 is the natural target because most Python files in the mod already use it, and this fixed Ruff parsing while preserving comments and leaving runtime code unchanged. This seems less risky than XML encoding edits so done for these py files.
